	<!-- Locked flight mini-map. This value is PER-DEVICE.

	     A value that is right on a phone is wrong on a 1024x720dp controller and vice versa;
	     the reasoning below transfers between screens, the number does not.

	     flight_resource_row_margin_end is DERIVED from this value: map size + 14dp, where the
	     14dp is the HUD column's paddingEnd. Change one and change the other, in EVERY bucket
	     that overrides either.

	     The HUD column is a fixed-height vertical LinearLayout: slider + EV scale + exposure
	     readout + weighted spacer + 5-line readout + gimbal + FAA line + THIS MAP. The map is
	     the last child, so when the column's contents exceed the screen height the weighted
	     spacer collapses to zero and the map is pushed off the bottom and silently clipped —
	     no error, no crash, just a half-map (the same failure class as the Home screen's
	     ENTER FLIGHT card).

	     Budget: everything above the map is ~233dp, or ~269dp while the IR palette button is
	     showing (it is in this column, below the exposure readout, and only visible in thermal
	     mode — so the worst case is thermal ON). At 269dp, a 130dp map needs 399dp of height,
	     160dp needs 429dp and the wide-screen 240dp needs 509dp. A Pixel 8 Pro in
	     landscape is ~448dp; the Smart Controller V3 is MEASURED at 720dp.
	     200dp here would need 449dp and overflow the Pixel by a hair. Don't raise it without
	     redoing that arithmetic.

	     NOTE the 429dp figure for the 160dp bucket sits only ~19dp under a Pixel-class 448dp
	     screen, and that headroom exists only while thermal is off. Anything further added to
	     this column will overflow small screens FIRST, and silently — the map just loses its
	     bottom. Measure before adding, and prefer the wide-screen bucket for new controls.

	     flight_map_size is the COLUMN width: it also sizes the EV slider, the EV scale row and
	     the exposure readout, so changing it moves more than the map. flight_map_height is the
	     map alone. They are equal here and in values-h440dp (square map); only the wide-screen
	     bucket makes the map taller than it is wide. -->
	<dimen name="flight_map_size">130dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="flight_map_height">130dp</dimen>

	<!-- flightResourceMonitorRow's marginEnd — see its own layout comment. MUST equal
	     flight_map_size + flightHudColumn's paddingEnd (14dp), so it stays pinned to the map's
	     left edge in every size bucket. A plain 144dp hardcoded into the layout is correct only
	     for THIS (base) bucket — it silently falls ~50dp short of the map's real edge on the
	     Smart Controller V3, which lands in values-w820dp where the map is 180dp, not 130dp.
	     Update alongside flight_map_size. -->
	<dimen name="flight_resource_row_margin_end">144dp</dimen>

	<dimen name="margin_84dp">84dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="margin_30dp">30dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="margin_50dp">50dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="margin_350dp">350dp</dimen>

	<!-- Flight-screen readout column text (Clock / SPI overlay text / gimbal pitch / FAA ceiling
	     / RTH altitude) — the flightReadoutText style in styles.xml. Base size matches hudText's
	     12sp, unchanged on smaller hardware (e.g. Smart Controller SE). See values-w820dp for
	     the Smart Controller V3 override: hard to read at 12sp on that screen. -->
	<dimen name="flight_readout_text_size">12sp</dimen>

	<!-- CrosshairView stroke widths — arms (outline/line) and the accuracy ring (ring/
	     ringOutline). Base values here are in PX, not DP, deliberately: they are raw
	     Paint.strokeWidth values (3f, 1.5f, 3f, 6f), so this bucket's on-screen appearance is
	     the same on every screen. Only values-w820dp (the Smart Controller V3) overrides them,
	     ~25% heavier — the reticle reads too fine at this screen's real size/viewing
	     distance. Read via Resources.getDimension(), which returns PX values as-is
	     with no density scaling, same reasoning as the raw-px choice. -->
	<dimen name="crosshair_arm_outline_width">3px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_arm_line_width">1.5px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_ring_width">3px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_ring_outline_width">6px</dimen>

	<!-- Black outline around HUD readout glyphs — see OutlinedTextView. This is
	     the VISIBLE width; the class doubles it, because a centred stroke hides its inner half
	     under the fill.

	     ⚠ PER-DEVICE, for the same reason flight_readout_text_size is. This base bucket is for
	     the smaller screens (and phones) where the readouts are 12sp: a stroke
	     that reads well at 18sp fills in the counters of 12sp glyphs and turns them to mud.
	     values-w820dp (the Smart Controller V3) carries the heavier value. Re-measure on a real
	     screen over a BRIGHT scene before changing either — that is the case this exists for.

	     ⚠ THIS IS THE STROKE WIDTH AND HALF OF IT FALLS INSIDE THE LETTER. Keep it near an
	     eighth of the text size. 1.8dp here, DOUBLED in the view, leaves about 1px of white
	     inside a 5px stem on the controller and the whole readout renders as black blobs.
	     1.5dp is 3px against this bucket's 24px text. -->
	<dimen name="hud_text_outline_width">1.5dp</dimen>

	<!-- Corner radius of a floating CONTROL on the flight screen: the toolbar capsules and the
	     mini-map's zoom button.

	     ⚠ TWO RADII, AND THE DIFFERENCE CARRIES MEANING (design decision, following TAK Aware's
	     system). A control the pilot TOUCHES is heavily rounded; a thing the pilot READS is
	     square or barely rounded — the mini-map frame has square corners, the readouts have no
	     backing at all. Do not split the difference: a 10 or 12dp radius reads as a consumer
	     card and tells the pilot nothing. -->
	<dimen name="hud_control_radius">20dp</dimen>

	<!-- Warning banner — PER-DEVICE. The text size, and the width the banner may take before
	     the text wraps. Sized for a 1024dp-wide screen; a 768dp screen needs its own values.
	     480dp keeps an open banner of five lines inside the left third of the picture; a
	     narrower banner does not get smaller, it gets TALLER, and height is what covers the
	     picture. The close button is the touch-target minimum, not the size of the glyph. -->
	<dimen name="flight_warning_text_size">15sp</dimen>
	<dimen name="flight_warning_max_width">480dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="flight_warning_close_size">34dp</dimen>


    <!-- ⚠ BOTH TOOLBAR CAPSULES MUST BE THIS TALL, AND IT IS A MINIMUM, NOT A HEIGHT.
         The two clusters hold different things, so they measure differently: the ACTIONS
         capsule's tallest child is the 46dp drop pin and the STATUS capsule's is a 34dp icon.
         Two capsules that begin on the same line and end on different ones read as a mistake.

         ⚠ IT IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN: the actions capsule's natural height, which is the drop
         pin plus the capsule's own paddingVertical on each side.

             46dp drop pin + 2 x 3dp paddingVertical = 52dp

         A value BELOW that does nothing at all === the actions capsule is already taller, and
         the status capsule stays short (at 40dp the capsules are not level).
         If the drop pin or the padding changes, this changes with them.

         A MINIMUM rather than a fixed height because either cluster may still grow: a longer
         signal readout, a taller button style, a density not yet seen. minHeight can only make
         a capsule taller, thus it can never clip its own content. -->
    <dimen name="hud_capsule_height">52dp</dimen>

    <!-- THE SHAPE OF EVERY TOGGLE PILL IN THE ACTIONS CAPSULE — AR, zoom, IR, lights, LIVE and
         REC. Three of those are shape drawables and two are canvas views that draw their own
         round rect, so the number lives here rather than in five places.

         ⚠ 8dp IS NOT hud_control_radius (20dp), AND THE DIFFERENCE IS DELIBERATE. The capsule
         is the container and takes the large radius; the pills INSIDE it take the small one. A
         pill at the container's radius reads as a second container rather than a control in
         one. This is the same two-radius rule the mini-map frame follows. -->
    <dimen name="hud_pill_radius">8dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="hud_pill_stroke">1.5dp</dimen>

